UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity of the complexes 1-6 were determined in terms of their partition coefficients between n-octanol and waterusing a modified “shake flask” method [41]. Octanol saturated water (OSW) and water saturated octanol (WSO) were prepared using analytical grade n-octanol (Merck) and double distilled water. In short, 5 ml solution of a complex in OSW was vortexed with same amount of WSO in a falcon tube for ∼15–20 min. The organic and aqueous phases of biphasic mixture were separated by centrifugation for ∼15–20 min at 3500 rpm. The concentrations of the complexes 1-6 in n-octanol and aqueous phases were determined using UV–vis spectroscopy. The partition coefficients were calculated by taking average of partition coefficients at three different complex concentrations."}]}